# Normalise every text file to LF in the working tree, on every platform.
#
# This is a correctness requirement, not a style preference. GitHub's Windows
# runners enable `core.autocrlf=true` system-wide, so without this file
# `actions/checkout` writes CRLF into the working tree while the committed blobs
# are LF. Prettier's default `endOfLine` is `"lf"`, so every checked-in file then
# fails `prettier --check` — which is exactly how the CI "Format check" step
# failed on 2026-10-20 with all 35 files reported unformatted at once.
#
# Pinning `eol=lf` here makes the working tree identical to the committed bytes
# regardless of the local `core.autocrlf` setting, so the same command gives the
# same result on Windows, macOS, and Linux.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be line-ending converted or diffed as text.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.gif binary
*.icns binary
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
*.sig binary
